  "chapter": {
    "number": 119,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(120) A Song of Degrees."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In my affliction I cried to the Lord, and he listened to me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver my soul, O Lord, from unjust lips, and from a deceitful tongue.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What should be given to you, and what should be added to you, for your crafty tongue?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Sharpened weapons of the mighty, with coals of the desert.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Woe is me, that my sojourning is",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 228
          },
          {
            "text": "prolonged; I have tabernacled among the tents of Kedar.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My soul has long been a sojourner;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I was peaceful among them that hated peace; when I spoke to them, they warred against me without a cause.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 228,
